OL,3,AShein aims for almost $27bn valuation
OL,4,Ain stock market debut
OL,5,
OL,6,FFast-fashion giant Shein says it plans
OL,7,Fto raise up to HK13.86bn (#1.3bn;
OL,8,F$1.77bn) when its shares start trading
OL,9,Fon the Hong Kong stock market on 1
OL,10,FSeptember.
OL,12,FIn a filing on Monday, Shein said it
OL,13,Fwill offer nearly 280 million shares
OL,14,Ffor between HK$47.60 and HK$49.50.
OL,16,FAt the top of the range, it would value
OL,17,Fthe firm at almost $27bn (#19.8bn). But
OL,18,Fthat is much lower than the $100bn
OL,19,Fvaluation it reached in a round of
OL,20,Fprivate fundraising in 2022, reflecting
OL,21,Fweaker sales growth and higher costs.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG9/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
